================================================================================
SPEECH RECOGNITION MODELS (optional, not stored in this repository)
================================================================================

The offline speech recognition path (-Pvosk=true) uses two acoustic models
from the Vosk project by Alpha Cephei Inc:

  vosk-model-small-pl-0.22       Apache License 2.0
  vosk-model-small-en-us-0.15    Apache License 2.0
                                 "Copyright 2020 Alpha Cephei Inc"

  Source: https://alphacephei.com/vosk/models

THESE MODELS ARE NOT REDISTRIBUTED HERE. They are downloaded from the address
above by tools/vosk-fetch.sh, which verifies the published archives against
pinned SHA-256 digests.

MODIFICATIONS MADE (required by Apache License 2.0, section 4b). tools/vosk-slim.py
rewrites one file of each model, graph/Gr.fst: the arcs of the language model are
removed and only its symbol table is kept, leaving a valid FST with a single final
state and no transitions. The application always builds its recognizers from an
explicit word grammar, so Vosk composes its own grammar FST with graph/HCLr.fst and
never traverses an arc of Gr.fst; it needs that file solely for the symbol table.
This removes about 34 MB (Polish) and 21 MB (English) per model. No other file of
either model is altered. The reasoning is documented in full at the top of
tools/vosk-slim.py.

The Android binding com.alphacephei:vosk-android:0.3.75 is also licensed under
the Apache License 2.0 and depends on net.java.dev.jna:jna:5.18.1, which is
dual-licensed under the Apache License 2.0 and the LGPL 2.1 or later; it is used
here under the Apache License 2.0.


